## PART B — ELEMENTAL IMPURITY (EI) BUGS (same Sitagliptin) could be product agnostic case too in the future

### EI-1. Abstract contradicts the Conclusion (P0, compliance-facing)
**What happens:** Abstract says confirmatory exhibit-batch testing is recommended for Pb/Cd/V/Ni/Li/Ba/Cr/Cu; Conclusion says no confirmatory testing required. All totals are <30% PDE, so the Conclusion is correct.
**Why:** the Abstract's testing sentence is a static template string, not driven by the computed `needs_confirmatory` flag that drives the Conclusion/Control-Strategy/Testing-Recommendation.
**Fix:** generate the Abstract's recommendation from the SAME computed `needs_confirmatory` boolean (and the same crossing-element list) used by the Conclusion. One source of truth reused across Abstract, Observation, Conclusion, Control Strategy, Testing Recommendation so they can never disagree.

### EI-2. Aerosil wrong values — limit column + phantom Class 2B/3 (drives the largest totals)
**What happens:** Aerosil shows Pb 1/As 2/Cd 1/Hg 3 (the ICH limits, not <-bounds) and Class 3 Cr 1100/Cu 300/Sn 600/Mo 300 that do not exist in the Evonik source.
**Why:** two errors — (a) the Class 1/2A values were read from the ICH-limit column instead of the Evonik `<`-bound column (Cd<0.5, Pb<0.5, As<1.5…), same wrong-column class as RS-1; (b) the Class 2B/3 values are fabricated/cross-read — the Evonik ICH Q3D statement explicitly says NO Class 2B/3 elements are present.
**Fix:** read Aerosil from the Evonik `<value` column and preserve `<` for conservative_bound; emit NO Class 2B/3 concentrations for Aerosil (all 0). Root-cause where Cr 1100 etc. came from (wrong-table/cross-material read). Expected: Aerosil Pb 0.5/As 1.5/Cd 0.5/Hg 3/Co 5/V 10/Ni 20; all 2B/3 = 0.

### EI-3. Croscarmellose unmatched → zeroed (multi-material annexure)
Same root cause and fix as RS-5: the IFF Cork PRDS covers MCC AND Croscarmellose; make the mapping many-to-many so Croscarmellose takes its Section-8 values (V<1.0, Ba<2.0, Cr<2.0) under conservative_bound instead of 0. Propyl gallate genuinely has no EI annexure → correctly 0.

