## PART C — DEG/EG BUGS (same Sitagliptin, standardized template run)

DEG/EG assessment logic is correct (Opadry Brown = EG source; all else No). Remaining defects:

### DEG-1. Material code misread (digit corruption)
Anhydrous Dibasic Calcium Phosphate rendered **100018292**; the CoA and Excel both say **100018232** (232→292). Even when the code IS provided cleanly in the template's Material-code column, a digit is corrupted downstream.
**Fix:** read the material code directly from the template's Material-code column verbatim; do not OCR-re-read or reconcile a value the Excel already supplies cleanly. Validate structurally and preserve exactly.

### DEG-2. Blank codes for materials whose code IS in the template
Sitagliptin, Croscarmellose, Propyl gallate, Mag stearate, Opadry show empty code cells though the template carries every one (350015984, 100003381, 100100325, 100014538, 100019237/238, 100100619).
**Why:** the DEG/EG parser is not wired to accept material codes from the composition Excel's Material-code column — it looks only in filenames/CoAs.
**Fix:** when the composition template carries a Material-code column, read each row's code from it into the output tables. Add the Excel Material-code column as a supported code source for DEG/EG (and RS/EI) composition parsing.

