## PART D — EXCEL GROUNDING IS TOO STRICT

The grounding failed on real DRL formula sheets and needed manual header edits. Two concrete gaps:

### D-1. Strength-column header vocabulary too narrow (the "For 100 mg/tab" failure)
**What happens:** `[RS] mode=insufficient_material_names_only` on the Sitagliptin formula sheet whose strength headers read **"For 100 mg/tab" / "For 50 mg/tab" / "For 25 mg/tab"** — even though quantities are filled. Removing "/tab" by hand made it run.
**Why:** `_STRENGTH_RE = r"^\s*\d+(?:\.\d+)?\s*mg\s*$"` matches only a bare "100 mg"; the leading "For " and trailing "/tab" both break it, so `_strength_columns` returns empty and the classifier falls to insufficient. `_QTY_HINTS` also lacks "mg/tab".
**Fix:** broaden strength detection to accept `(?:for\s+)?\d+(?:\.\d+)?\s*mg\s*(?:/\s*(?:tab|tablet|capsule|unit|vial))?` (case-insensitive, optional "For", optional "/unit" suffix); `_strength_columns` still extracts the numeric mg. Add "mg/tab" to `_QTY_HINTS`. Product-agnostic; bare "N mg" behaviour unchanged.

### D-2. Grounding must be a strong prior, never a gate; L1 must fully lock or fall to L2
**What happens:** the deterministic fast-path either mis-reads or bails on off-template real sheets (merged two-row headers, "For N mg/tab", extra Material-code column) instead of gracefully handing to the LLM.
**Fix:** the Layer-1 deterministic fast-path must claim a workbook ONLY when it locks cleanly and completely (sheet-type + all quantity/strength columns resolved); ANY ambiguity, partial match, or unrecognized-but-present quantity column → fall through to Layer-2 LLM alignment BEFORE ever returning `insufficient_material_names_only`. Never hard-fail to "names only" when a filled quantity/strength table is present in any recognizable form. Fuzzy/tolerant sheet-type and column matching (accept "OSD (1)", merged headers, shifted rows, stray columns, "For N mg/tab").

